      "id": 1,
      "text": "Leaside Station opened in September 1894, its name honoring founder William Lea.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leaside"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1892 a junction was built in Leaside, creating the Don Branch railway that ran south along the Don River toward Toronto’s original Union Station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leaside"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Leaside Station carried CP passenger trains for more than 75 years until 1970, when the service was discontinued and the station closed shortly after.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://leasideresidents.ca/leaside-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Leaside was the first town in Ontario to be fully planned on paper before any houses were built.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
